To implement bubble sort in C++ for the given JSON data, you can follow these steps:

1. Define a function to perform bubble sort on the array:
```cpp
void bubbleSort(int arr[], int n) {
    bool swapped = true; // flag to check if any swaps were made
    int end = n - 1; // last index of array

    while (swapped) { // loop until no more swaps are needed
        swapped = false; // reset flag

        for (int i = 0; i < end; i++) { // iterate through array from left to right
            if (arr[i] > arr[i+1]) { // swap elements if current is greater than next
                int temp = arr[i];
                arr[i] = arr[i+1];
                arr[i+1] = temp;
                swapped = true; // set flag if swap was made
            }
        }

        --end; // decrease end index to avoid comparing already sorted elements
    }
}
```

